LOCAL1="A 3D program is shown flat"
LOCAL2="%s is shown flat: the desktop's X server could not show the two pictures of its 3D window together, so the window shows the left picture alone. 3D returns by itself when the window can show both again. Update Sparky Stereo OS and log in again; if the program stays flat, report it with the program's name. Mesa says: %s"
LOCAL3="OpenGL programs draw on the processor"
LOCAL4="OpenGL programs draw on the processor in this session: OpenGL was set to run on the graphics card's Vulkan driver (zink), which needs an X server with DRI3, and the desktop's X server (Xwayland) runs without 3D acceleration. Programs work, more slowly. Log out and in again; if it repeats, look at the graphics driver on the Graphics page of System Settings. Mesa says: %s"
